# Simulator item-port rule

Before adding or changing an item handler, read:

- `js/pages/sim/AGENTS.md`
- `docs/sim/sim-item-porting.md`
- the exact `tools/game-extract-full/Items/**/*.gd` source and its inheritance
- the called shared `tools/game-extract-full/Core/` behavior

Do not begin from a tooltip, catalog field, another handler, or an audit count.
The game extract is authoritative.

## Hard requirements

- Work one item or a source-proven tight family at a time. Do not rewrite a
  whole port-wave module to add a single item.
- Map every lifecycle hook, parameter, target/geometry rule, consume/reset,
  and source call before coding. If any is unknown, leave the row incomplete
  and report it; do not guess.
- Use shared engine helpers for damage, stacks, cooldowns, board targeting,
  events, and seeded RNG. Do not directly mutate visible actor state or add
  item-specific event/log ordering hacks.
- Keep per-copy state on `piece`, not module globals or an item-id map. Test
  player and opponent paths.
- Register a catalog id exactly once. Never leave an undefined import/export
  or duplicate registry entry.
- Visible behavior must emit the canonical event data required by Combat Log,
  Damage Meter, HUD, scrubber, and JSON export.
- Add a focused regression that checks source behavior, causal order, both
  sides, and applicable UI projections.
- Run `node --check` on changed modules, the focused family smoke,
  `node scripts/audit-sim-gd-parity.mjs --require-triage`,
  `node scripts/audit-sim-gd-calls.mjs`, and
  `node scripts/sim-continuous-audit.mjs --check --family <smoke>`.
- Never make a test pass by deleting checks, widening fixture bands, clearing
  mismatch fields, or marking the ledger/backlog complete from handler presence.

When source semantics require a missing shared helper or core behavior, stop
the item port and create a named shared-engine follow-up with the source path
and minimal reproduction. An explicitly incomplete port is safer than a
plausible approximation.
